+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ a: [1, 2] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/a/-", value: 3 },
+  { op: "test", path: "/a/0", value: 1 },
+  { op: "move", from: "/a/1", path: "/b" },
+]); // { a: [1, 3], b: 2 }
+```
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`
+in order and returns the result as a new value; the document and the patch are never modified. It throws a
+`JsonPatchError` when the patch is malformed or any operation fails (missing target, bad array index, failed
+`test`, ...), and then returns nothing. JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386) is not supported.
