+## Why
+
+Our services need to change stored and exchanged JSON documents with the standard patch format instead of ad-hoc code. The library already resolves JSON Pointers (RFC 6901), which JSON Patch (RFC 6902) is built on.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, implementing RFC 6902 with the operations `add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy` and `test`.
+- It returns the patched document as a new value and never mutates its input (neither the document nor the patch).
+- It throws a `JsonPatchError` when the patch is malformed or any operation fails; no partial result is returned.
+- Document the feature in `README.md`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying an RFC 6902 JSON Patch to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+None. The existing `json-pointer` requirements are unchanged; only its pointer parsing is reused internally.
+
+## Impact
+
+- Code: new `src/patch.ts`, a small internal export of pointer parsing from `src/pointer.ts`, new export in `src/index.ts`, new tests in `test/`.
+- No new dependencies. No breaking changes.
+- Out of scope: JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386), patch generation (diff), URI fragment pointers.
